  "H2466": {
    "orig": "חלד",
    "tran": "chêled",
    "phon": "khay'-led",
    "bdbd": "1. Heled = \"transitorio\"\n2. The term \"Heled\" is used to describe a phenomenon that lasts for a brief period of time.\n3. It can be applied to various fields such as science, technology and medicine.\n4. For instance, in psychology, the concept of Heled refers to temporary feelings or emotions that come and go.\n5. In biology, Heled describes a stage in the development of certain species that is characterized by rapid growth and change.\n6. In medical terms, Heled can refer to a temporary condition or illness that resolves itself over time.\n7. The concept of Heled has many practical applications and can be used to develop new treatments and therapies.\n8. For example, understanding how to manage Heled in psychological disorders could lead to more effective treatment options.\n\n9. Heled is often contrasted with permanent or long-term changes, which have a lasting impact on an individual or system.\n10. In conclusion, the concept of Heled is an important area of study that can be applied to various fields and has many practical implications.",
    "orin": "the same as H2465",
    "twot": "None",
    "posp": "Nombre Propio Masculino",
    "sdef": "La traducción es:\n\n1. Lo mismo que H2465; cheled, un israelita:\n2. - Heled.",
    "atra": "kld",
    "shor": "chêled. Heled = \"transitorio\""
  },
