  "G1691": {
    "orig": "ἐμέ",
    "tran": "eme",
    "phon": "em-eh'",
    "thad": "1. Yo, mí, mismo, etc.\n2. These pronouns are special because they refer to the speaker themselves.\n3. They can be used in various sentences and contexts.\n4. For example:\n5. \"I am going to the store.\" (yo voy a la tienda)\n6. \"Me and my friend are going to the movies.\" (mí y mi amigo vamos al cine)\n7. \"Myself, I don't think that's a good idea.\" (para mí mismo, no creo que sea una buena idea)\n8. The word \"myself\" can also be used reflexively.\n9. For example:\n10. \"I cut myself shaving this morning.\" (me corté al afeitarme esta mañana)\n11. In this case, the reflexive pronoun is used to emphasize the action of cutting oneself.\n12. These special pronouns are important in many languages and cultures.",
    "orin": "a prolonged form of G3165",
    "tdnt": "None",
    "posp": "",
    "sdef": "Una forma prolongada de G3165; yo: - Yo, yo, mi (-misma).",
    "atra": "eme",
    "shor": "Yo, mí, mismo, etc."
  },
