  "G2258": {
    "orig": "ἦν",
    "tran": "ēn",
    "phon": "ane",
    "thad": "1. Yo era, etc.\n2. In a small town, there were some interesting people.\n3. They had strange habits and customs.\n4. One of them was an old man named George.\n5. He lived in a tiny house at the edge of the town.\n6. George was very different from other people.\n7. He loved to collect strange objects.\n8. His house was filled with weird things.\n9. There were shells, rocks, and feathers everywhere.\n10. Some people thought he was crazy.\n11. But George didn't care what they thought.\n12. He liked being unusual.\n13. One day, a group of children discovered his house.\n14. They had heard stories about George's collection.\n15. The children were amazed by all the strange things they saw.\n16. They asked George to show them more.\n17. He was happy to share his treasures with them.\n18. From that day on, George became a popular figure in town.\n19. Children would visit him every week.\n20. He loved having an audience for his stories and treasures.",
    "orin": "imperfect of G1510",
    "tdnt": "None",
    "posp": "Verbo",
    "sdef": "Imperfecto de G1510; Yo (tú, etc.) era (eras o eramos): - + acuerdo, ser, X tener (+ cargo de), sostener, utilizar, era (-t), éramos.",
    "atra": "hn",
    "shor": "Yo era, etc."
  },
